  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on skewness, which in this case favors Lottery A due to its higher probability (80%) of the best possible outcome (0). However, the individual does not mention or appear to consider the concentration of probability on favorable outcomes (i.e., zero) as a decisive factor. Instead, the individual focuses on the size of the potential loss and the small difference in loss probabilities, indicating a loss-aversion or minimax-type reasoning rather than a skewness-based evaluation. There is no indication that the individual assessed which lottery has more probability mass on favorable outcomes, which is central to the skewness reason. The justification is based on a trade-off between loss size and probability, not on the distributional shape or skew. Therefore, the reasoning process described does not align with the skewness-based decision rule.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
